#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0252-B expect=violation domain=ADSL
#note "PARAMCD, AVAL and BASE are three names from the rule's 44-name concrete membership list - concrete prohibited BDS variables leaking into ADSL, the realistic contamination case. Since Fix #270 (ruling M2-D3) the Check tests the variable NAME (varname() in [...] plus one regex per template family, no wildcards left), routes as Variable Metadata Check / Record via evaluateMetadataNative and emits ONE finding per offending variable -> THREE violations, pinned by variable_name only (no row= pin: Violation.row carries the colIndex). Formerly the D9 PREDICTED-RED pin of finding AD0252-B-F1 - pre-#270 the wildcard-carrying Check went whole through WildcardExpander and a NoMatch dropped the rule with its concrete arms; the ruling removed that failure by construction and this scenario flipped green."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 3
#expectViolationAt variable_name=PARAMCD
#expectViolationAt variable_name=AVAL
#expectViolationAt variable_name=BASE
dataset ADSL structure=ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
col BASE    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | 30 | 28
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALB | 31 | 28
